  "status": "N2_CONDITIONAL_CONFLICT_U_R_AND_LOCAL_U_G_OPEN",
  "phase": "Exploratory manually authored extensions on already documented exposed contexts. No new fixed corpus experiment or selected meaning.",
  "parent": "research_registry/proposals/production_origin_supply_20261003/DAL_TASK_AND_NOMINAL_DRAFT_20261015.json",
  "question": "How can the proposed common free/bound markers combine without deleting occurrences, overwriting roles or silently supplying a new head/governor?",
  "retained_observations": [
    "All readers have exact f11r.4 dchol chy kchy dy daiin with definite inner gaps. IT/ZL mark paragraph end; RF flags remain unset.",
    "IT f56r.17 has exact chokeey qokcheey schey daiin dy. ZL instead has d~aiin and RF d aiin; no pooled literal daiin. The IT line is not paragraph-final.",
    "f45r.9 kol dy is exact across readers. dor or is literal only inIT: ZL @201;or or andRF dor @221;r retain their entities.",
    "f14v.6 has one whole dydydy inIT/RF; ZL has dy~dy~dy with uncertain small gaps. The literal repeated region is stable; three independently delimited operator words are not. The shorthand definite-pipe rendering in1200 must not be used as evidence of definite inner gaps."
  ],
  "N2": {
    "status": "CONTRADICTED_UNDER_DECLARED_SAME_HEAD_SINGLE_SLOT_CONTRACT",
    "new_contract": "A nominal record has one referent x and one optional role field. R_or,R_dy,R_daiin are explicitly pairwise distinct. Each licensed marker consumes the current nominal record: set its role if empty, accept unchanged if equal, reject if different. Every marker in one uninterrupted adjacent run acts on that same record. No unmarked reset, new head, clause break or secondary word class is inserted.",
    "change_from_N1": "N1 originally returned ArgSpec rather than another nominal input. N2 explicitly extends the input type to marked records and permits repeated agreement. It does not retroactively validate the parent type rule.",
    "f11r4": [
      "kchy supplies the hypothesized nominal record x_kchy.",
      "dy assigns R_dy.",
      "daiin demands R_daiin != R_dy.",
      "CONFLICT at IT2a|f11r.4|G005."
    ],
    "f56r17_IT": [
      "schey supplies the hypothesized nominal record x_schey.",
      "daiin assigns R_daiin.",
      "dy demands R_dy != R_daiin.",
      "CONFLICT at IT2a|f56r.17|G005."
    ],
    "dor_or": "With dor treated as an opaque nominal head, only the free or assigns a role. Under a separately assumed productive dor=d+or analysis, inner and outer or agree on the same role. Neither possibility proves the segmentation.",
    "scope_of_failure": "A conditional contradiction of this type/identity/attachment conjunction, not proof that the manuscript words are markers of one head. If a word starts another expression, marks another level or denotes content, that is a different construction. Distinct spellings alone did not establish distinct roles.",
    "decision": "Do not export this exclusive-slot grammar or repair it by a local overwrite/reset. No census or parameter search is needed for the displayed conditional conflicts."
  },
  "U": {
    "name": "Shared participant with cumulative role obligations",
    "new_type": "Bundle(N,x,e,Phi,Trace), containing a nominal description, its referent, a governing-relation placeholder, role obligations and every written occurrence.",
    "marker_rule": "For any licensed s, append Arg(e,R_s,x) to Phi and the occurrence to Trace. Keep N,x and e fixed throughout that nominal marker run. Output another Bundle. Free and licensed fused s use the same rule.",
    "mixed_markers": "N dy daiin requires N(x) AND Arg(e,R_dy,x) AND Arg(e,R_daiin,x). The same participant occupies two roles of the same governing relation.",
    "repeated_markers": "N or or repeats the same role condition. The two written occurrences remain in Trace; no extra person, amount or execution follows.",
    "governor_limit": "e is an unresolved binding obligation to a written governing expression, not a new event conjured by the marker. Different nominal occurrences have unresolved governor/referent identities; no paragraph-wide same-event assumption is imported.",
    "order": "The role conditions are conjunctive and their order alone does not change their truth. The ordered textual trace is retained. This is not a claim that manuscript word order is globally irrelevant.",
    "informative_future_consequence": "If a bound governing relation requires the two roles to have explicitly different participants, the same-x U binding fails. No such relation or participant inequality is currently read.",
    "role_semantics": "Arg(e,R_s,x) abbreviates value(e,R_s)=x for one single-valued argument slot. The three role identifiers are distinct in U but may share a participant value. Single-valued slots are a new model assumption, not a recovered native frame."
  },
  "R": {
    "name": "Ordered relational nominal composition",
    "new_type": "A nominal description is a unary predicate N. Every marker s is a noun-forming relational operator M_s:N->N.",
    "marker_rule": "M_s(N)(y) iff exists x [N(x) AND r_s(y,x)]. The relation r_s and its direction remain fixed across uses but their actual content is unassigned. Read consecutive postfix markers left to right; free and licensed fused forms use the same operation.",
    "mixed_markers": "N dy daiin yields exists x,z [N(x) AND r_dy(z,x) AND r_daiin(y,z)]. Reverse order yields r_daiin first, then r_dy.",
    "repeated_markers": "N or or has two r_or links. No idempotence, deletion or forced distinctness of intermediate participants is assumed.",
    "reference_limit": "The outer description may denote a different participant or class from the original N. D remains an inner argument in a derived DAL expression; it is not automatically the outer referent. Quantified variables do not assert creation of new physical objects.",
    "content_limit": "The fixed relational formula supplies a composition discipline, not concrete relation meanings. Arbitrary unknown relations and successful bracketing do not identify a historical reading or explain manuscript frequencies.",
