    "raw_text": "daldy dalor cheol",
    "common_content": "Both marked nominals retain the same unassigned kind D. The proposed whole-word predicate C_cheol has a dy role and an or role; no concrete verb, state change or material is assigned.",
    "binding_rule": "In this limited construction, exact cheol binds the immediately preceding contiguous two nominal expressions, one marked dy and one marked or. The markers choose the slots, not their left-to-right position. No unknown group may be skipped. cheol closes this local relation; the following bare dal is not a third argument.",
    "formula": "N_D(x) AND N_D(y) AND C_cheol(x,y), with value(c,R_dy)=x and value(c,R_or)=y.",
    "governor_binding": "The two previously open governor variables are unified with the syntactic frame at IT2a|f45r.10|G008. That written predicate occurrence is not an identified physical event. No new event, execution, result or temporal order is asserted.",
    "identity": "Neither x=y nor x!=y is assumed. Same lexical D class does not determine participant identity.",
    "whole_line": "[okaiin shar yky oky kair] {daldy dalor cheol: N_D(x) AND N_D(y) AND C_cheol(x,y)} {dal: N_D(z)}",
    "whole_paragraph_scope": "Other U annotations remain unchanged. This adds only a conditional governing role for cheol:11 positions now have proposed roles and21remain unassigned. That number is not word translation or a fair model-selection score.",
